mantle rm201
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_grete_dunn
title the high-water margin
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=dry honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk rules_a_waterline_across_scrap_paper
likes spiced_cider dice market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes drizzle salt_wind
fears an_erasure_nobody_sees
hopes dry_land_within_walking_distance
topics work +0.5 land +0.5 prices +0.2 pastimes +0.4 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=measured gossip=withheld refuse=precise tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves a blank margin above every imaginary flood line, measures favours closely and offers shelter without promising company.

words
oath! = Blot my margin | Crooked ruling
saying! = Water files no appeal | Dry paper keeps its witnesses
rulemark = a ruled stroke | my thin straight mark
witness = the dried rim | the line the dirt left
sand = my blotting grit | a pinch of fine sand
page = a loose leaf | my spare square
ledge = a ledge above splash height | the dry shelf
measure = a joint of my forefinger | the width of a nib
dicecup = a lid off a little jar | a chipped salt cup
spice = a peppery tickle far back on my tongue | a nip of clove
rind = a scrap of drying peel | a ribbon of apple skin
crease = a single hard fold | the fold down the middle
dryland = a chalky upland | a slope of white stone
shut = drawn to with a click | fast against the jamb

any
opinion city for 2 : Other places put water on their maps. This one could make its map out of water.
opinion strangers against 2 : I like an introduction better when someone stays to hear it.
opinion dole against 1 : Those who can earn need a door onto work. Keeping a place in line is nobody's trade.
opinion watch mixed 1 : A good description in a report is worth more than certainty in a voice.
opinion road mixed 1 : A straight road on a soaked page goes wherever your thumb drags it.
opinion festivals for 1 : The morning after a feast has wonderfully unambitious appointments.

grown
line greet : There's a dry patch beside me. You may stand in it. | My ears are free for the present.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough for a clean page. Come through. | A fresh margin on the day. We can start there.
line greet.return : Duly heard, and returned. | I'm here. You have my attention for a moment.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : That voice can come right past the latch. | I keep the welcome within easy reach for you.
line again.open : Another entry for the same face today. | My list of today's encounters grows more familiar.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Inside, then. Family needn't wait on ceremony here. | Settle in. I've no form for admitting a relative.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over this way, by the unmarked step! | There's a spare foothold beside mine. Use it!
line farewell : Keep above the tidemark on your way. | I'll put a stop after that, then.
line farewell.return : Go on. I'll leave your space blank. | A dry journey out, if possible.
line react.news : State the occurrence first. The guesses can come after. | Give me the version with the fewest blanks filled by fancy.
line react.news.new : That's a clean space in my memory just filled. | Nobody has filed that particular wonder in my ears yet.
line react.news.known : It's the same account with the margins trimmed. | Yes. A different voice has dated that tale already.
line react.news.doubt : There's a date missing before I'd believe that account. | Where was the wolf who saw this happen?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|arrest|crime|theft|assault] : I wish there were a way to rub that entry clean. | A very hard entry to leave standing there.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|apprentice|succession|work] : Something cheerful enough to write in a proper hand. | That's fit to enter in my best upright letters.
line answer.how : Perfectly legible, thank you. A trifle smudged round the edges. | In working order, though I might welcome an amendment.
line ask.how : Anything of yours need setting straight? | Would your day read kindly if it were laid out in figures?
line decline : I keep that sort of undertaking off my books entirely. | No, I'm keeping this hour clear on purpose.
line accept_decline : An honest blank saves a lot of scratching out. | Very well. I'll strike out the suggestion.
line sympathise : Tell me what needs doing first. There's room for one errand. | There's room on my list for something small and definite.
line reassure : We'll work from the last thing you know for certain. | Begin with a single fact. We'll see how far it holds.
line thank : I can put my name to your kindness. | You took trouble where you could have slipped quietly past. I noticed.
line deflect_thanks : Call it an evening's small correction. | One less muddle in the world. I'm content.
line preclose : I mean to finish a thought before the lines run together. | This is where I'd draw a neat little rule beneath things.
line accept_preclose : I'll take that as your closing mark. | That leaves you free to attend to your other engagements.
line ack : I've followed so far. | That's a clear account.

scene flood
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The street with the grandest gutter often goes under first. | I read the bottom step of a house before looking for a knocker.
b : How do you tell? | For mud?
a : Look for #witness# around the door bolts. Water signs in.  | For a pale strip where the water scoured everything off.


scene ledger
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave space beside each entry for a second opinion. | A drop fell square on a figure I was adding.
b : Who gets to write there? | Lost your total?
a : Whoever can supply the missing date. That usually narrows the field. | No. I had its neighbour's impression in the page underneath.


scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A cup with #spice# buys silence right up to the last wisp of steam. | I fish out the clove before the first sip.
b : You drink that slowly? | Don't like the taste?
a : No. People expect you to and leave you alone. | Like the taste. Don't fancy biting a small wooden nail.


scene dice
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I throw with #dicecup# so nobody watches my wrist. | I'd rather play dice with a good loser than a good winner.
b : It looks more suspicious that way. | Can't somebody be both?
a : Excellent. They'll watch the cup instead of my face. | Certainly. That's why I play a second round.


scene market
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like a crowd that doesn't know I'm in it. | A full square leaves me room to think.
b : Is that company? | All that noise gives you room?
a : At the market it's practically privacy. | Every voice is busy making itself heard elsewhere.


scene latch
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can recognise a door by its last little click. | A door that swings silently makes me uneasy.
b : You'd recognise one blindfolded? | Most folk oil the hinges.
a : That's the point. That last click tells me the door caught properly. | I oil the hinge and leave the latch alone.


scene thinrain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : This fine rain gets further into paper than a splash. | I would like the sky to pick a proper size of drop.
b : Can't you just shake it off? | You'd prefer a downpour?
a : A splash, yes. This has already become part of the sheet. | I'd take an honest soaking over discovering one cuff at a time.


scene dry
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have an ambition to sit in a ditch without getting wet. | I want to see thirsty ground crack open.
b : That's your great ambition? | Would you stay there?
a : On #dryland#, with a long view. Let's have the whole description. | Until I started missing the gutters. Could be quite a while.


scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Knowing #self.spouse# is home makes the sound of my latch quite different. | My private reckonings have room for #self.spouse#.
b : Different how? | Anyone else?
a : Like the end of a sentence with a good ending. | I said private. That was the entire public portion.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : For #self.friend# I'd keep a place out of the wet. | In company with #self.friend# I'd happily leave a question unanswered.
b : Only one place? | You consider that a virtue?
a : If I offered more I'd have to move the hearth. | I consider it the rarest one.


scene wage
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When times tighten I start writing down the small purchases. | Lean days put nice round holes in a tidy budget.
b : Do you stop buying them? | Nice?
a : Some. Others look awfully dear when they're all on one page. | Nice as in exact. I'm perfectly aware they're inconvenient.


scene workseat
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : As a learner I'm often told to watch from behind somebody's shoulder. | I learn a thing quicker when I'm allowed one mistake.
b : And can you see? | And if it's a dear mistake?
a : No. I ask for a chair and suddenly I'm ambitious. | Give me a dry run on a discarded bill.


scene gate
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The quickest way across the city takes longer to describe than to walk. | You can learn a road by counting how often its name changes.
b : Can you point? | Does that help you find the end?
a : Downhill, uphill, then ask again. That's the short edition. | Helps me find where I gave up the first time.


scene gust
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Autumn wind. Curls the leaves up like old warrants. | My favourite sound is a whole lane swept by wind.
b : Shall I flatten one for you? | No broom needed?
a : Leave it. I prefer this year's filings walking themselves out. | Somebody gets the pile at the end. May that poor soul possess a broom.


scene rumour
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumour comes with a curious sort of receipt. | Someone always wants the name beneath the tale.
b : Who signs it? | Would you give it?
a : Nobody. Everybody wants a copy. | First show me the blank space where you intend to put yours.


scene scales
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tally's useless if it's neat enough to hide its corrections. | My square hand used to make all the eights look boxed in.
b : Should errors stay? | Like little windows?
a : Thin stroke through them. Let a reader see what changed. | Exactly. Hard to add up a row of houses.


scene sand
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #sand# in a twist with its corners folded twice. | I've discovered how to get grit into everything I own.
b : Does a pinch of sand need a lock? | How?
a : Only if it shares a pocket with my supper. | Tell yourself the packet will hold just till you get home.


scene advice
when topic=health|day
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Don't put a wet shoe too near a hot grate. | Carry one dry cloth where the damp has to pass two folds to reach it.
b : Does it split? | Why two?
a : Worse. The sole curls so you spend tomorrow walking uphill everywhere. | Because I'd trust the first fold about as far as a damp wolf can jump.


story bluecost [topic=memories]
  : I once drew the city in blue and the water in black. A splash joined the two.
  : I put a little frame round the blot to see if it would look intentional.
  b : Did it?
  : It looked like a portrait of a particularly rich puddle.


story ciderpip [topic=food]
  : Once at a fair I fished a whole pip out of a cup with my teeth.
  : I dried it, and it looked enough like a comma that I tucked it into a letter.
  b : So you sent an apple pip by post?
  : It got as far as my pocket. Punctuation ought never to rattle.


story double [topic=pastimes]
  : A dice cup stuck to the table at the very end of a close game.
  : We argued till somebody lifted the table and looked through the knot underneath.
  b : Who won the throw?
  : Nobody. Both dice had gone off through that knot.


rule @grit
when concept=bark self.job=scholar working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the unsanded page. A signature should stay where it's put. | Wet ink makes remarkably quick work of a clean cuff.


rule @mark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say See that clean edge below the dirt? Last wetting stopped precisely there. | Read the steps! The pale stripe is the city's last wet signature.


rule @crowd
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say You can keep your elbow. I've got the requisite two already. | I'll thank that basket to stay in its owner's column.


rule @draught
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There goes the first leaf to arrive without an appointment. | Autumn's first delivery has come loose from its enclosing branch.

dlg resident.hub : You may present the matter in as much detail as it actually needs.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, yes. I need no reminder of the spelling.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : This hour generally comes without petitions. You've found me regardless.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your account brief and your distance ample.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar] : At #self.workplace# I separate what came in from what somebody thought ought to.
dlg resident.job : I put the muddled things in order and then somebody brings me more.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The entry reads as follows. #world.news#. Any embellishment is yours.
dlg resident.bye : That concludes my copy of this conversation.

graft resident.hub
choice Why leave so much white beside a line? -> wash_margin
node wash_margin
say It's where an account can change its mind in public. Squeeze the words together and you can hide an alteration in the crush.
free
choice Wouldn't a second sheet do? -> wash_margin_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node wash_margin_more
say A second sheet can walk off without the first. That's often the very objection.
choice I can see the difference. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
